### Double-click scenario

Two quick clicks on the final button must not create two official forwarding operations.

### Two-reviewer scenario

Two School staff members attempt forwarding simultaneously.

Exactly one authorized logical forwarding result must be committed for that unit/season.

### Network timeout scenario

The request may have succeeded even if the client did not receive the response.

The UI must check the canonical server status before inviting an unsafe retry.

Do not blindly submit again.

### Partial failure

A failure while forwarding must not leave:

- Half the selected applications forwarded.
- A batch marked successful with missing members.
- An attached decision reference inconsistent with the forwarded selection.
- The City queue showing an incomplete unofficial result.

Do not claim ACID transaction coverage unless actually verified.

